feat: the four summary tiles now filter the list

They read as controls and did nothing. The brief asks for no interaction, so this
is not a requirement: it removes a dead affordance rather than adding a feature.

ToggleGroup with type="single", so the semantics are a radio group: Tab reaches it,
arrows move between filters, Space selects. Pressing the active one again keeps it
selected instead of clearing to a state the tiles do not display.

"Đã nộp" includes late submissions. The brief lists A04 as Đã nộp with Nộp trễ as
an annotation, so filtering it out of its own status would contradict the badge on
the same row. matchesFilter carries that rule and is exported so a test can assert
it without a DOM.

The filter can only narrow what the server sent: it runs on the four rows already
scoped to S01, so a bug here hides a row and cannot reveal B01.

Selected state: data-[state=on] draws a 2px dark ring and a 4% wash. The default
Radix tint was invisible on a near-white page, which I confirmed by reading
computed styles rather than by eye.

Cost: the ToggleGroup primitive adds 67 KB raw / 24 KB gzip to the client bundle,
which is the real price of the control.

Tests 32 to 36. Verified by clicking through the running build at 1280 and 400px,
and by keyboard: Tab, ArrowRight, Space.
